B.FT=new A.V(12,"Build the double threat",B.y,"A single threat is an invitation to block. Two threats made by one move end the game, because they only get one turn. Look for the square that finishes two lines at once.",B.af,B.JA,2,null,B.l,"Column 3 leaves the amber sunbursts with two separate squares that each complete a four, and the teal diamonds cannot cover both. Note that neither threat existed before the move: the fork was created, not found.",!0,B.i,null,null)
